  "question": "Look up general recalls for a 2020 Toyota Corolla.",
  "identity": "tech_demo",
  "answer": {
    "status": "answered",
    "text": "There are three general recalls for the 2020 Toyota Corolla: 1) Recall 19V877000 for rear seat belt assemblies with a dual-mode locking mechanism that may not lock as intended, potentially increasing injury risk in a crash. Toyota will inspect and replace assemblies as needed free of charge. 2) Recall 20V682000 for a low-pressure fuel pump inside the fuel tank that may fail, causing the engine to stall and increasing crash risk. Toyota will replace the fuel pump assembly free of charge. 3) Recall 23V865000 for a short circuit in the Occupant Classification System sensor that may prevent the front passenger air bag from deploying, increasing injury risk. Dealers will inspect and replace the sensor as necessary free of charge.\n\nSource: live; observed: 2026-09-27T14:21:16.014276+00:00. Showing 3 of 3 returned campaign records. General year/make/model campaign records only. These do not establish VIN-specific eligibility, repair completion, or that a vehicle is safe to drive. An empty result does not prove there are no recalls.",
